From: Linghao Zhang <linghao.zhang@kemaro.ch>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:50:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] lec-mtk1200: target the root node in the memory overlays

The memory-{2G,4G,8G}.dts overlays use target-path = "/soc", but the kernel's
memory node is at the root (/memory@40000000). The overlay only adds an unused
/soc/memory@40000000, so MemTotal never changes (3.7 GiB on an 8 GB unit).
Target "/" so the overlay replaces the real memory node.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Linghao Zhang <linghao.zhang@kemaro.ch>
---
 memory-2G.dts | 2 +-
 memory-4G.dts | 2 +-
 memory-8G.dts | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/memory-2G.dts b/memory-2G.dts
--- a/memory-2G.dts
+++ b/memory-2G.dts
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
 
 / {
 	fragment@0 {
-        target-path = "/soc";
+        target-path = "/";
 		__overlay__ {
 			memory@40000000 {
 				device_type = "memory";
diff --git a/memory-4G.dts b/memory-4G.dts
--- a/memory-4G.dts
+++ b/memory-4G.dts
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
 
 / {
 	fragment@0 {
-        target-path = "/soc";
+        target-path = "/";
 		__overlay__ {
 			memory@40000000 {
 				device_type = "memory";
diff --git a/memory-8G.dts b/memory-8G.dts
--- a/memory-8G.dts
+++ b/memory-8G.dts
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
 
 / {
 	fragment@0 {
-        target-path = "/soc";
+        target-path = "/";
 		__overlay__ {
 			memory@40000000 {
 				device_type = "memory";
